{"changes":["eka-cli v1.27.0 (PR #44): `eka agents-md --nested --write|--check [--json]` extends the existing agents-md command (root behaviour unchanged without --nested). Nested-file rule: a directory D that directly holds tracked files and whose subtree matches \u003e=1 constraint's `appliesTo` gets D/AGENTS.md carrying the SAME marker-delimited managed block as the root (BuildAgentsMDBlock + MergeAgentsMD) over ONLY D's bound index; pure-ancestor dirs and empty bindings write nothing. Host shims (`--host claude|cursor|opencode`): .claude/rules/\u003cslug\u003e.md (paths:) and .cursor/rules/\u003cslug\u003e.mdc (globs:) per bound dir, emitted ONLY when the host's config dir exists; opencode is a documented no-op. New bootstrap/nested.go + bootstrap/shim.go; cmd/agents_md.go orchestration.","eka-cli v1.27.1 (PR #45): fixes a real defect found in merge verification — the projection wrote 1071 AGENTS.md files inside exchange/snapshots/** (constraint adr:027 globs the snapshot tree), corrupting the SEALED transport tree: exchange.LoadSnapshot rejects unknown entries, so `--nested --check` then exited 2 and `eka verify` FAILed agents-md-drift + snapshot-integrity. Fix: a named constant bootstrap.SnapshotDir (\"exchange/snapshots\") and an explicit candidate-dir exclusion; the sealed tree is never a projection destination (its constraints still count for the root block, untouched). Verified: 0 files under exchange/snapshots, `--nested --check` exit 0, `eka verify` PASS.","Version: anvil.yaml + README CLI axis -\u003e v1.27.1 (EKA Standard 1.7, eka-core v1.13.0 unchanged). No core change; no new dependencies (reuses pathglob + exchange.LoadSnapshot)."],"role":"implementation","summary":"M2 (sto:path-scoped-projection) is complete. The binding index is now projected to where the agent reads: `eka agents-md --nested` generates a per-directory AGENTS.md naming only the constraints bound to that subtree, and per-host rule shims are emitted for a declared host that is configured. The projection is generated and drift-checked (byte-identical regeneration; a hand-edited nested file fails --check), never writes into the sealed snapshot tree, and writes nothing where no constraint binds.","tests":["AC1 (byte-identical regen + hand-edit fails): TestAgentsMDNestedScoped, TestAgentsMDWriteThenCheck.","AC2 (host shims only when configured; unconfigured skipped; opencode no-op): TestAgentsMDNestedHostClaude.","AC3 (two subtrees bound by different constraints name only their own): TestAgentsMDNestedScoped (fixture with a/** vs b/**).","AC4 (empty bindings write no file): TestAgentsMDNestedScoped (unbound dir + no-file dir).","Sealed-tree invariant (v1.27.1): TestAgentsMDNestedSealedSnapshot — asserts NO nested file at or under exchange/snapshots even when a scope globs it; negative control (exclusion disabled) reproduces the exact defect (3 files leaked, --check exit 2).","Gates: `go test ./bootstrap/ ./cmd/ -count=1` green; `anvil pipeline ci` success (712.2s) — format/vet/windows-cross-compile/verify/unit-tests(-race); verify PASS agents-md-drift + snapshot-integrity. Releases v1.27.0 and v1.27.1 published.","AC5 (the A/B spike) recorded separately as eka/spk:path-scoped-projection (derives-from this work item): 96/96 code files covered, 0 governing-constraint misses, 1-\u003e0 steps, 8,596 B (8 nested files) covers the whole code tree vs 119,374 B of per-file queries — positive on coverage/steps/cost, honest caveat that directory-granularity over-names (median 18 vs 3); the projection is a passive safety net, not a substitute for `eka context --for`."]}